  "body": "<p>Representing two generations of Chinese tennis, wild cards Sun Xinran and Zheng Qinwen thrilled the China Open fans on Saturday as they booked their spots in the third round of their home tournament.</p>\n<p>Junior World No. 1 Sun stunned No. 27 seed Cristina Bucsa 6-4, 7-5 in 1 hour and 31 minutes to become the first 2010-born player to win a completed match at WTA 1000 level or above. The 16-year-old, fresh off the girls' title at the US Open, is making her WTA main-draw debut this week. She'll next face another player who knows a thing or two about making a mark at a young age -- No. 3 seed Coco Gauff, the 2024 Beijing champion.</p>\n<p>Olympic gold medallist Zheng, who put together a memorable run to the US Open quarterfinals as a qualifier, continued her resurgence by advancing when No. 15 seed Anna Kalinskaya was forced to retire due to illness trailing 6-7(4), 6-4, 3-0. She'll next face No. 18 seed Marie Bouzkova for the first time after the Czech player ended Seoul champion Kimberly Birrell's six-match winning streak 6-4, 6-4.</p><div class=\"articleWidget center\">\n        <aside class=\"instagram-post embeddable-widget embeddable-widget--floating embeddable-widget--centered-mobile \"><blockquote class=\"instagram-media\" data-instgrm-captioned data-instgrm-permalink=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DeCAKFuxxbu/?utm_source=ig_embed&amp;utm_campaign=loading\" data-instgrm-version=\"14\" style=\" background:#FFF; border:0; border-radius:3px; box-shadow:0 0 1px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.5),0 1px 10px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.15); margin: 1px; max-width:540px; min-width:326px; padding:0; width:99.375%; width:-webkit-calc(100% - 2px); width:calc(100% - 2px);\"><div style=\"padding:16px;\"> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DeCAKFuxxbu/?utm_source=ig_embed&amp;utm_campaign=loading\" style=\" background:#FFFFFF; line-height:0; padding:0 0; text-align:center; text-decoration:none; width:100%;\" target=\"_blank\"> <div style=\" display: flex; flex-direction: row; a