79,41.056 516.623,37.899 C516.755,34.978 517.244,33.391 517.654,32.338 C518.197,30.938 518.846,29.942 519.894,28.894 C520.942,27.846 521.94,27.196 523.338,26.654 C524.393,26.244 525.979,25.756 528.898,25.623 C532.057,25.479 533.004,25.448 541,25.448 C548.997,25.448 549.943,25.479 553.102,25.623 C556.021,25.756 557.607,26.244 558.662,26.654 C560.06,27.196 561.058,27.846 562.106,28.894 C563.154,29.942 563.803,30.938 564.346,32.338 C564.756,33.391 565.244,34.978 565.378,37.899 C565.522,41.056 565.552,42.003 565.552,50 C565.552,57.996 565.522,58.943 565.378,62.101 M570.82,37.631 C570.674,34.438 570.167,32.258 569.425,30.349 C568.659,28.377 567.633,26.702 565.965,25.035 C564.297,23.368 562.623,22.342 560.652,21.575 C558.743,20.834 556.562,20.326 553.369,20.18 C550.169,20.033 549.148,20 541,20 C532.853,20 531.831,20.033 528.631,20.18 C525.438,20.326 523.257,20.834 521.349,21.575 C519.376,22.342 517.703,23.368 516.035,25.035 C514.368,26.702 513.342,28.377 512.574,30.349 C511.834,32.258 511.326,34.438 511.181,37.631 C511.035,40.831 511,41.851 511,50 C511,58.147 511.035,59.17 511.181,62.369 C511.326,65.562 511.834,67.743 512.574,69.651 C513.342,71.625 514.368,73.296 516.035,74.965 C517.703,76.634 519.376,77.658 521.349,78.425 C523.257,79.167 525.438,79.673 528.631,79.82 C531.831,79.965 532.853,80.001 541,80.001 C549.148,80.001 550.169,79.965 553.369,79.82 C556.562,79.673 558.743,79.167 560.652,78.425 C562.623,77.658 564.297,76.634 565.965,74.965 C567.633,73.296 568.659,71.625 569.425,69.651 C570.167,67.743 570.674,65.562 570.82,62.369 C570.966,59.17 571,58.147 571,50 C571,41.851 570.966,40.831 570.82,37.631\"></path></g></g></g></svg></div><div style=\"padding-top: 8px;\"> <div style=\" color:#3897f0; font-family:Arial,sans-serif; font-size:14px; font-style:normal; font-weight:550; line-height:18px;\">View this post on Instagram</div></div><div style=\"padding: 12.5% 0;\"></div> <div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: row; margin-bottom: 14px; align-items: center;\"><div> <div style=\"background-color: #F4F4F4; border-radius: 50%; height: 12.5px; width: 12.5px; transform: translateX(0px) translateY(7px);\"></div> <div style=\"background-color: #F4F4F4; height: 12.5px; transform: rotate(-45deg) translateX(3px) translateY(1px); width: 12.5px; flex-grow: 0; margin-right: 14px; margin-left: 2px;\"></div> <div style=\"background-color: #F4F4F4; border-radius: 50%; height: 12.5px; width: 12.5px; transform: translateX(9px) translateY(-18px);\"></div></div><div style=\"margin-left: 8px;\"> <div style=\" background-color: #F4F4F4; border-radius: 50%; flex-grow: 0; height: 20px; width: 20px;\"></div> <div style=\" width: 0; height: 0; border-top: 2px solid transparent; border-left: 6px solid #f4f4f4; border-bottom: 2px solid transparent; transform: translateX(16px) translateY(-4px) rotate(30deg)\"></div></div><div style=\"margin-left: auto;\"> <div style=\" width: 0px; border-top: 8px solid #F4F4F4; border-right: 8px solid transparent; transform: translateY(16px);\"></div> <div style=\" background-color: #F4F4F4; flex-grow: 0; height: 12px; width: 16px; transform: translateY(-4px);\"></div> <div style=\" width: 0; height: 0; border-top: 8px solid #F4F4F4; border-left: 8px solid transparent; transform: translateY(-4px) translateX(8px);\"></div></div></div> <div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; flex-grow: 1; justify-content: center; margin-bottom: 24px;\"> <div style=\" background-color: #F4F4F4; border-radius: 4px; flex-grow: 0; height: 14px; margin-bottom: 6px; width: 224px;\"></div> <div style=\" background-color: #F4F4F4; border-radius: 4px; flex-grow: 0; height: 14px; width: 144px;\"></div></div></a><p style=\" color:#c9c8cd; font-family:Arial,sans-serif; font-size:14px; line-height:17px; margin-bottom:0; margin-top:8px; overflow:hidden; padding:8px 0 7px; text-align:center; text-overflow:ellipsis; white-space:nowrap;\"><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DeCAKFuxxbu/?utm_source=ig_embed&amp;utm_campaign=loading\" style=\" color:#c9c8cd; font-family:Arial,sans-serif; font-size:14px; font-style:normal; font-weight:normal; line-height:17px; text-decoration:none;\" target=\"_blank\">A post shared by WTA (@wta)</a></p></div></blockquote>\r\n<script async src=\"//www.instagram.com/embed.js\"></script></aside>\n</div><p>Sun had already delivered an eye-catching performance in her first round, winning nine straight games in a blaze of winners before Eva Lys retired trailing 6-1, 3-0 due to a foot injury. Against a stronger and healthier opponent in Bucsa, the teenager soon showed she could back up her opening result in a full match.</p>\n<p>Indeed, it was Sun's composure in closing it out that was most impressive. After erasing an early 2-0 deficit in the second set, she advanced to a game of victory at 5-4 -- but Bucsa, swarming the net, raised her game to level at 5-5. Momentum threatened to turn the Spaniard's way as she held a break point for 6-5. Sun responded brilliantly, swatting a forehand winner down the line to stave it off. A game later, she sealed victory on her first match point by threading a forehand pass.</p>\n<p>\"<span data-olk-copy-source=\"MessageBody\">I feel really excited before the match,\" Sun said afterwards. \"I know she is really good player. I just want to play my best tennis. First set start really hard because I was little bit nervous. After I feel better and better. Just like this.\"</span></p>\n<p>Currently ranked No. 582, Sun is guaranteed to make her Top 500 debut following Beijing. She'll become the third 2010-born player to do so, following Memphis champion Kristina Liutova (currently No. 119) and Jana Kovackova (currently No. 451).</p><div class=\"articleWidget center\">\n\n</div><p>During her US Open run, Zheng attributed her uptick in form to <a href=\"https://www.wtatennis.com/news/4573453/how-one-training-block-allowed-zheng-qinwen-to-rediscover-her-game-ahead-of-us-open-quarter-run\">the intense training block in Florida</a> that she underwent after losing in Toronto qualifying to Lanlana Tararudee. That's shown not just in her results, but her scorelines. Seven of her last nine matches have gone to three sets, and she's won six of those.</p>\n<p>Against Kalinskaya, Zheng piled on the first-strike pressure early. In a remarkable game at 2-2 in the first set, she fired five aces, eventually tallying 13 overall. But there was also a lack of consistency that meant she was unable to close out a 5-3 lead, with Kalinskaya finding better serves when it matters to snatch the tiebreak.</p>\n<p>The Roland Garros quarterfinalist had the opportunity to press home her advantage when she held two break points for 2-0 in the second set, but was unable to take either. Zheng continued to slam a succession of return winners off the Kalinskaya delivery, and was eventually rewarded with the break for 4-3 -- and this time, she made no mistake in closing the set out.</p>\n<p>Kalinskaya received a medical timeout after the first game of the decider, and lasted just two more games before pulling the plug.</p>\n<p>Though pleased with how she responded in the second set, Zheng wasn't entirely satisfied with her performance.</p>\n<p>\"I was 5-3 up, then I couldn't get the first set when I had my serve on my hand,\" she said in her press conference. \"<span data-olk-copy-source=\"MessageBody\">I kind of feel like I make the match difficult today 'cause I got lot of break point in the first set ... </span>So takes a while to change a bit the mentality in the second set.</p>\n<p>\"But I was just happy that I'm able to get the match, even she retired. But I felt like the match is quite on my dynamic.\"</p>",
